name:
  type: string
  unique: true
  id: true

labels:
  type: string
  arity: 1..*
  description: |
    Label(s) used to select the host(s) onto which to install this feature.

    A host is targeted when it carries at least one of these labels.

    **Label absorption**: when none of the cluster's hosts carry a matching
    label, the feature is instead deployed to every sole node (controllers
    running in --single mode).  This lets sole nodes act as a catch-all for
    features that haven't been explicitly routed yet.  Once a dedicated
    non-controller host with a matching label is added to the cluster, the
    explicit match takes precedence and the sole node no longer receives
    the feature.

locations:
  type: uri
  arity: 0..*
  description: |
    Filepaths containing necessary installation
    scripts and configurations for deployment

install-cmds:
  type: bash
  arity: 0..*
  description: |
    List of installation commands. Runs
    sequentially. All filepaths defined under
    `locations` are mounted in the execution
    directory throughout deployment only

init-cmds:
  type: bash
  arity: 0..*
  description: |
    List of initialization commands, executed
    once, needed to execute the feature at
    runtime


  